{"key": "6216", "mpkey": "2342", "stat": "A", "schd": "A", "code": "MRKT 492H", "section": "001", "crn": "15072", "title": "CONSUMER BEHAVIOR", "session_html": "Full Term (11 week; Fall/Winter/Spring/Summer) (09-23-2026 to 12-04-2026)", "hours_html": "4", "rpt_for_credit": "", "campus": "Oregon State - Corvallis", "sche_type_clss_fild": "Lecture", "inst_mthd": "In-Person Section", "grade_mode": "Normal Grading Mode", "status": "Open", "max_enroll": "10", "enrollment": "3", "ssbsect_seats_avail": "7", "waitlist_capacity": "5", "ssbsect_wait_count": "0", "ssbsect_wait_avail": "5", "cross_list_max_enroll": "", "xlist_wait_cap": "", "ssbxlst_seats_avail": "", "description": "Understanding the processes that lead to purchase, so as to improve decisions on segmentation and the appropriate marketing mix for each segment. How consumers and households make decisions, and why different individuals/groups make different decisions. Application of behavioral science concepts at individual, subcultural and cultural levels. Effects of consumerism and regulation also are considered.", "registration_restrictions": "<p class=\"prereq\">Prerequisites: <a href=\"/search/?p=BA%20223\" data-action=\"result-detail\" data-group=\"code:BA 223\" >BA 223</a>, <a href=\"/search/?p=BA%20223H\" data-action=\"result-detail\" data-group=\"code:BA 223H\"  class=\"notoffered\">223H</a>, <a href=\"/search/?p=BA%20390\" data-action=\"result-detail\" data-group=\"code:BA 390\" >390</a> or <a href=\"/search/?p=BA%20390H\" data-action=\"result-detail\" data-group=\"code:BA 390H\"  class=\"notoffered\">390H</a>.<br/>A minimum grade of C is required in <a href=\"/search/?p=BA%20223\" data-action=\"result-detail\" data-group=\"code:BA 223\" >BA 223</a>, <a href=\"/search/?p=BA%20223H\" data-action=\"result-detail\" data-group=\"code:BA 223H\"  class=\"notoffered\">BA 223H</a>, <a href=\"/search/?p=BA%20390\" data-action=\"result-detail\" data-group=\"code:BA 390\" >BA 390</a> and <a href=\"/search/?p=BA%20390H\" data-action=\"result-detail\" data-group=\"code:BA 390H\"  class=\"notoffered\">BA 390H</a>.</p><p class=\"cls\">Students with a term class standing of Freshman, Sophomore or Junior may <strong>not</strong> enroll.</p><p class=\"maj\">Enrollment is limited to students with a program in:<ul><li>Apparel Design (400)</li><li>Merchandising Management (416)</li><li>Interior Design (458)</li><li>Marketing (799)</li><li>Marketing (814)</li><li>Professional Sales (817)</li><li>Digital Marketing Analytics (903)</li><li>Market Res & Consumer Analytic (904)</li><li>Design & Innovation Management (912)</li><li>Product and Merchandising Mgmt (A014)</li></ul></p><p class=\"deg\">Enrollment limited to students in a Honors Bachelor of Arts, Honors Bachelor of Fine Arts, Honors Bachelor of Music or Honors Bachelor of Science degrees.</p>", "corequisites": "", "department_approval_required": "", "recommendations": "", "fees": "", "attribute_description": "Honors Course Designator (HNRS)", "books_html": "", "clssnotes": "<p>Honors students should register for section 001. \nNon-Honors Dean's Academy students should \nregister for section 002.\n<p><a href=\"http://oregonstate.edu/registrar/rtfiles/q.html?\n:&202701&MRKT&492H&001&15072\" target=\"blank\">Textbooks</a></p>", "meeting_html": "<div class=\"meet\">TR 8am-9:50am<span class=\"meet-room-202701\"> in <a href=\"https://map.oregonstate.edu/?id=2243#!m/1027675?share\" target=\"_blank\">AUST 440 - Austin Hall 440</a></span><span class=\"meet-dates\"> (9/23 to 12/4)</span></div>", "exams_html": "", "instructordetail_html": "<div class=\"instructor-detail\">Jason Stornelli</div>", "all_sections": "<div class=\"course-sections\" role=\"grid\" aria-readonly=\"true\"><div role=\"row\"><div role=\"columnheader\" scope=\"col\">CRN</div><div role=\"columnheader\" scope=\"col\">Section #</div><div role=\"columnheader\" scope=\"col\">Campus</div><div role=\"columnheader\" scope=\"col\">Meets</div><div role=\"columnheader\" scope=\"col\